---
import { ArrowRight, BookOpen, CodeXml, MessageCircle } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CallRibbon from '../components/CallRibbon.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/catalog';
import { communityLinks } from '../lib/community';
---
<BaseLayout title="Getting started" description="Find a reusable Power Platform snippet, understand the pattern, and adapt it to your app, agent, or automation.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Small steps. Useful patterns." title="Skip the blank canvas." description="Find the little building block your idea is missing. Explore the pattern, try it in a development environment, and make it your own." portrait={3}><a class="button button--primary" href={sitePath('/#sample-catalog')}>Find a snippet <ArrowRight size={17} /></a></PageHero>
  <section class="content-section content-section--soft"><ol class="container steps-grid">
    <li><h2>Find your building block.</h2><p>Browse by product, category, or maker. Open a snippet to see its preview, source, authors, and original README.</p></li>
    <li><h2>Understand the pattern.</h2><p>Read prerequisites and setup instructions. Check required controls, connectors, permissions, licensing, and any experimental features before using it.</p></li>
    <li><h2>Adapt and test.</h2><p>Follow the snippet's instructions to copy a formula, reuse a component, import a topic, or try a desktop flow. Test with your own data in a development environment.</p></li>
  </ol></section>
  <section class="container content-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose the path that fits</p><h2>Small pieces. Your bigger idea.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="resource-grid">
      <article class="resource-card"><CodeXml size={29} /><h3>Patterns, not prescriptions</h3><p>Snippets are focused examples, not complete supported applications. The README explains what to copy or import and how to configure it. Preserve attribution when sharing adaptations.</p><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/#sample-catalog')}>Explore the patterns <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></article>
      <article class="resource-card"><BookOpen size={29} /><h3>Learn the why</h3><p>Use official documentation alongside the snippet. Understand its formulas, properties, and integration points rather than copying code without checking its assumptions.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/power-platform/">Power Platform documentation <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></article>
      <article class="resource-card"><MessageCircle size={29} /><h3>Learn together</h3><p>For product and how-to questions, start with the Power Platform Community forums. Report reproducible snippet bugs in the repository, with the snippet name and reproduction steps.</p><a class="text-link" href={communityLinks.forums}>Ask the community <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container content-section two-columns">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Room to experiment</p><h2>Keep your learning safe.</h2><p>Use development or test environments, review permissions and connector costs, and follow your organization's data and security policies. Never include secrets or production data in shared snippets.</p><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/contributing/')}>Share what you learn <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Need the whole solution?</p><h2>Take the next step.</h2><p>The companion Power Platform sample gallery has community-built apps, automations, agents, and solutions. Snippets are your small building blocks; samples show how the pieces come together.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://pnp.github.io/powerplatform-samples/">Explore the sample gallery <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></div>
  </section>
  <CallRibbon />
</BaseLayout>
